  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, though improving internal space standards, would result in an intrusive living conditions for occupants by virtue of the increased number and scale of fenestration to the principle elevation. The proposed windows would front directly onto the public realm encouraging overlooking into habitable rooms and resulting in a loss of privacy for occupants.&amp;nbsp;The development would be contrary to Policy 57 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (LP1) (2024) and Supplementary Planning Document&#x27; Residential Extensions and Alterations&#x27; (2010).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The proposed development, by virtue of its bulk, scale and use of material, is not considered to contribute positively to the streetscene and has failed to respond to the existing character of the area. The proposed development is not contextualized within the setting and would result in a dominant and uncharacteristic addition that is widely visible in the streetscene. The proposed extension would result in the loss of the gap at first floor level between existing 2 and 3 storey built form, which is a positive townscape feature. The proposal therefore conflicts with Policy 53 of the Waltham Forest Local Plan (LP1) (2024) and The National Planning Policy Framework 2021 (achieving well designed places), The National Design Guide: Creating Well Designed Places (2019) and Living with beauty: report of the Building Better, Building Beautiful Commission (2020), together with the relevant parts of the London Plan which seek to ensure new development responds positively to context and character.&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
